{"id": "tea:astapahuda:darsana.2", "source": "src:astapahuda", "location": {"ref": "darsana.2"}, "paraphrase": "Dharma has right faith (darśana) as its root, taught the Jina to his disciples; hearing this with your own ears, do not revere one without right faith.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "terms": ["trm:samyag-darsana"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-jewels"], "notes": "'daṃsaṇamūlo dhammo'.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:astapahuda:sutta.18", "source": "src:astapahuda", "location": {"ref": "sutta.18"}, "paraphrase": "The monk has the form of a newborn child; he does not accept even a sesame husk in his hands; if he takes little or much, he goes to the lowest (nigoda) births.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ethics", "dispute"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "terms": ["trm:acela", "trm:aparigraha"], "obstacles": ["obs:parigraha"], "concepts": ["cpt:monastic-nudity"], "disputes": ["dsp:monastic-nudity"], "notes": "Verse number moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:astapahuda:sutta.23", "source": "src:astapahuda", "location": {"ref": "sutta.23"}, "paraphrase": "In the Jina's teaching one who wears clothes is not liberated even if he were a Tīrthaṅkara; nakedness is the path to liberation, all others are wrong paths.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["dispute", "karma-liberation"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "terms": ["trm:acela", "trm:digambara"], "concepts": ["cpt:monastic-nudity"], "disputes": ["dsp:monastic-nudity"], "notes": "Verse number moderate confidence; the classic Digambara statement.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:astapahuda:sutta.24", "source": "src:astapahuda", "location": {"ref": "sutta.24"}, "paraphrase": "In women, in the private parts, between the breasts, at the navel and in the armpits subtle living beings are said to arise; how then can they have full renunciation (pravrajyā)?", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute", "body-layers"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "concepts": ["cpt:strimukti"], "disputes": ["dsp:women-caste-liberation"], "notes": "Recorded as the text states it (one of the Digambara arguments against women's full renunciation); verse number low confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
